    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent my whole life thinking i was destined for something massive. coding, competitions, just constant grinding to be the best. but i just hit this wall. i realized i'm just... average. i'm just another dev. i'll never be a maverick or a legend. honestly, it feels like i've wasted every single second of my life just to end up being nothing special. being mediocre feels like a slow death.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of \"mediocrity\" is incredibly painful in a highly competitive world like tech, and it is the very real \"impostor syndrome\" trap that even top 1% engineers enter after they give up trying to be \"the best.\"\n\nConsider that \"the best\" is a moving target set by millions of efforts daily, and your self-worth is not tied to being a \"maverick\" or a \"legend.\"\n\nMany of the most successful people in your field you consider \"average\" because the noise of constant grinding can make everyone feel the same.\n\nYou are not \"nothing special,\" just a content and capable human who might benefit from taking a step back to focus on what you love rather than just the \"end the self\n</think>\n\nI am thinking",
